Author: Eran Assaf <assaferan@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 29 13:01:43 2026 +0300

    PROTOTYPE (do not merge): integrality as an acceptance criterion in the form search
    
    Makes the Borcherds form search reject an (infty, other_pts) triple whose solve has
    no INTEGRAL solution, and take the solution from IsConsistent over Z rather than
    Solution over Q.  ~8 lines at the Solution call.
    
    33_2 goes from NONINTEGRAL to oo:INTEGRAL all:INTEGRAL.  The trace shows the search
    walking past the bad divisors instead of committing to the first one:
    
        key -1:  [-12,-4] false -> [-88,-4] false -> [-132,-4] TRUE  accepted
        key -2:  [-12,-4] false -> [-88,-4] false -> [-148,-4] TRUE  accepted
    
    A valid choice existed all along; the old search accepted the first divisor
    admitting a merely rational solution and never looked further.  Keys 9..15 are
    intsol true on every triple, confirming again that only the free-choice divisors
    were ever at fault.  The divisor assertion below still passes, so the forms this
    builds have correct divisors AND integral principal parts.
    
    BUT INTEGRALITY IS NOT SUFFICIENT.  Sweeping 33_2 against the fixed forms fails
    EARLIER than before -- "RationalNumber: s does not represent a rational number" at
    gtsweep.m:52, before HauptmodulM0Residuals.  Unfixed 33_2 gave a rational but
    inconsistent table; fixed 33_2 gives a table that is not rational at all.  So
    non-integrality predicts failure, but integrality does not predict success, and
    33_2 carries a second independent defect.  Do not read this as unblocking the
    backlog.
    
    Why this is not merge-ready:
      * it recomputes keys 9..15 identically for every candidate triple (visible as the
        repetition in fix_33_2.log) -- correct but wasteful, hoist before shipping;
      * the PROBE printf is unconditional and must become a vprintf.  Note that
        `assigned` does NOT see top-level variables from inside a package intrinsic, so
        a `magma PROBE:=1` flag silently never fires here.
    
    Next diagnostic, not yet done: dump the raw abs_tab values for fixed 33_2 before
    RationalNumber and test whether they are quadratic irrationalities.  A sqrt(2)
    would point at a half-integral m=0 multiplier for the new forms -- a different bug.
    Measure it rather than assuming it.
    
